WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.710
By the end of the 1500s, firewood and
charcoal in Britain cost twice as much as

2
00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.970
coal for the same energy.

3
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.250
Steam engines kept improving.

4
00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.850
Coal burned per horsepower-hour
fell from 45 pounds to 2.

5
00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:20.130
The Industrial Revolution began in
Britain in the 18th century, then spread.

6
00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.790
Yet those coal fires helped
redraw the map of Africa.

7
00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:25.190
How could that be?

8
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.750
In this mission, you'll find out
why industry began in Britain,

9
00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:32.490
and how it moved people
from fields to cities.

10
00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.370
Then you'll trace how industry
spread, from Chicago to Japan,

11
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:39.690
and what it meant for places far away.

12
00:00:39.740 --> 00:00:44.490
Your mission: explain how burning coal
in British factories helped redraw the

13
00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.640
map of Africa.
